<!-- Aura-SOC - rule 100807 (level 13). Domain: soc_selfcheck,wazuh,
     Naming convention and load-order trap: see rules/README.md -->
<group name="soc_selfcheck,wazuh,">

  <!-- Kernel audit EXPLICITLY DISABLED, seen at the heartbeat: the status
       command reports `audit_enabled=0` (a real 0, not an empty value). Someone
       (or something) switched auditing off - every auditd rule (1006xx/1007xx)
       is now inert. This is the hostile case T1562.001.

       Split out of 100801 (2026-07-31): 100801 used to match both the empty
       value (auditd absent) and `=0` (disabled) at level 13, which flooded on
       auditd-less hosts. 100801 now keeps only the empty/absent case at MEDIUM;
       this rule carries the genuine disable at HIGH.

       Complements 100805 (CONFIG_CHANGE): 100805 is immediate and carries the
       responsible auid, but only fires if the agent was already up when the
       switch happened and the event was not lost. This heartbeat rule catches
       the state even when audit was turned off BEFORE the agent started, or the
       CONFIG_CHANGE was missed - the two are not duplicates.

       Mutually exclusive with 100801 by value (`0` here, empty there): load
       order does not arbitrate between them. -->

  <rule id="100807" level="13">
    <if_sid>100800</if_sid>
    <match type="pcre2">audit_enabled=0\b</match>
    <description>Blind sensor: kernel audit explicitly disabled (audit_enabled=0 at heartbeat)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1562.001</id>
      <id>T1562.006</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
